What is the difference between /bin/bash and /bin/sh?
Initially they were thesame thing 
/bin/sh is the original Bourne shell interface defined by the POSIX standard, while /bin/bash (the Bash) is an enhanced shell that adds many extra features.
/bin/sh is a POSIX-compliant Bourne shell used for portable system scripts, while /bin/bash is an enhanced shell with additional features like arrays, better
scripting capabilities, and interactive improvements.

To switch to insert mode press esc button and i
To save and quit :wq!
